#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:34
msgid "Summary of Theory"
msgstr "理論の概要"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:36
msgid ""
"Here, we will briefly summarize the theory behind variationally enhanced "
"sampling (VES). For an full overview of VES, you should read the [original "
"paper](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.113.090601), a review in a [book "
"chapter on VES](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-44677-6_50), or a recent "
"[enhanced sampling review](https://doi.org/10.33011/livecoms.4.1.1583) that "
"includes discussion about VES."
msgstr ""
"Variationally Enhanced Sampling (VES) "
"の理論を簡単にまとめます。全体像を把握するには、[原著論文](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.113.090601)、[VES"
" についての書籍の章](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-44677-6_50)、または VES も扱う最近の "
"[Enhanced Sampling の総説](https://doi.org/10.33011/livecoms.4.1.1583) "
"を読んでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:38
msgid "VES is based on the the following functional of the bias potential:"
msgstr "VES は BiasPotential の次の汎関数に基づきます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:48
msgid ""
"where $\\mathbf{s}$ are the CVs that we are biasing, "
"$p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ is a predefined probability distribution "
"that we will refer to as the target distribution, and $F(\\mathbf{s})$ is "
"the free energy surface. This functional can be shown to be convex and to "
"have a minimum at:"
msgstr ""
"ここで $\\mathbf{s}$ は Bias を加える CV、$p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"は事前に定義する確率分布で Target Distribution と呼び、$F(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"は自由エネルギー表面です。この汎関数は凸で、次の条件で最小になることを示せます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:55
msgid ""
"The last equation states that when we minimize the functional $\\Omega [V]$,"
" we can obtain the free energy surface from the bias potential (and the "
"target distribution). We can choose the target distribution "
"$p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ at will and it is the CV distribution that "
"we obtain when minimizing $\\Omega [V]$."
msgstr ""
"この式は、汎関数 $\\Omega [V]$ を最小化すると BiasPotential と Target Distribution "
"から自由エネルギー表面を得られることを示します。Target Distribution $p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"は自由に選べ、$\\Omega [V]$ を最小化したときに得られる CV 分布になります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:60
msgid ""
"We put the variational principle to practice by expanding $V(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"in some basis set:"
msgstr "変分原理を実際に使うため、ある Basis Set で $V(\\mathbf{s})$ を展開します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:65
msgid ""
"where $f_i(\\mathbf{s})$ are the basis functions and the "
"$\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ are the coefficients in the expansion."
msgstr "ここで $f_i(\\mathbf{s})$ は Basis Functions、$\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ は展開係数です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:67
msgid ""
"We then need to find the coefficients $\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ that minimize "
"$\\Omega [V]$. In principle one could use any optimization algorithm. In "
"practice the algorithm that has become the default choice for VES is the so-"
"called [averaged stochastic gradient descent "
"algorithm](http://papers.nips.cc/paper/4900-non-strongly-convex-smooth-"
"stochastic-approximation-with-convergence-rate-o1n.pdf). In this algorithm "
"the $\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ are evolved iteratively according to:"
msgstr ""
"次に $\\Omega [V]$ を最小化する係数 $\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ "
"を求めます。原理的には任意の最適化アルゴリズムを使えます。実際に VES の標準となっているのは [Averaged Stochastic "
"Gradient Descent](http://papers.nips.cc/paper/4900-non-strongly-convex-"
"smooth-stochastic-approximation-with-convergence-rate-o1n.pdf) "
"と呼ばれるアルゴリズムです。$\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ を次のように反復更新します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:80
msgid ""
"where $\\mu$ is the step size, $\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)}$ is the "
"running average of $\\boldsymbol\\alpha^{(n)}$ at iteration $n$, and "
"$\\nabla\\Omega(\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)})$ and "
"$H(\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)})$ are the gradient and Hessian of "
"$\\Omega[V]$ evaluated at the running average at iteration $n$, "
"respectively. The behavior of the coefficients will become apparent in the "
"examples below."
msgstr ""
"ここで $\\mu$ は Step Size、$\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)}$ は反復 $n$ における "
"$\\boldsymbol\\alpha^{(n)}$ "
"の累積平均です。$\\nabla\\Omega(\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)})$ と "
"$H(\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}^{(n)})$ はそれぞれ、反復 $n$ の累積平均で評価した $\\Omega[V]$ "
"の勾配と Hessian です。係数の挙動は以下の例で明らかになります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:87
msgid ""
"As said above, we can choose the target distribution "
"$p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ at will. The most simple choice would be a "
"uniform target distribution. However, it has been found more optimal to "
"employ the so-called well-tempered distribution (see "
"[here](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076)):"
msgstr ""
"上述のとおり、Target Distribution $p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"は自由に選べます。最も単純なのは一様分布ですが、Well-tempered Distribution "
"を使う方がよいことがわかっています（[こちら](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076) を参照）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:95
msgid ""
"where $\\gamma$ is the so-called bias factor and $P(\\mathbf{s})$ is the "
"unbiased CV distribution. Therefore the well-tempered distribution is the "
"unbiased distribution with enhanced fluctuations and lowered barriers. This "
"is the same distribution as sampled in well-tempered metadynamics. The "
"advantages of this distribution are that the features of the FES (metastable"
" states) are preserved and that the system is not forced to sample regions "
"of high free energy (that can represent un-physical configurations) as it "
"would if we had chosen the uniform target distribution. There is a caveat "
"though, the well-tempered $p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ depends on "
"$F(\\mathbf{s})$ that is the function that we are trying to calculate. One "
"way to approach this problem is to calculate $p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$"
" self-consistently (see [here](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076)), "
"for instance at iteration $k$:"
msgstr ""
"$\\gamma$ は Bias Factor、$P(\\mathbf{s})$ は Unbiased な CV 分布です。したがって Well-"
"tempered Distribution は、揺らぎを増やし Barrier を下げた Unbiased 分布で、Well-tempered "
"Metadynamics が Sampling するものと同じです。FES の特徴（準安定状態）を保持し、一様な Target Distribution"
" を選んだ場合のように、高自由エネルギー領域（非物理的な Configuration の場合もある）の Sampling "
"を強制しない利点があります。ただし、Well-tempered の $p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ は、これから計算する"
" $F(\\mathbf{s})$ に依存します。この問題には、$p_{\\mathrm{tg}}(\\mathbf{s})$ "
"を自己無撞着に計算する方法があります（[こちら](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076) を参照）。例えば反復"
" $k$ では次のようになります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:110
msgid "where:"
msgstr "ここで、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:114
msgid ""
"Normally $p^{(0)}(\\mathbf{s})$ is taken to be uniform. Therefore the target"
" distribution evolves in time until it becomes stationary when the "
"simulation has converged. It has been shown that in some cases the "
"convergence is faster using the well-tempered target distribution than using"
" the uniform $p(\\mathbf{s})$ (see "
"[here](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076))."
msgstr ""
"通常、$p^{(0)}(\\mathbf{s})$ は一様とします。そのため Target Distribution "
"は時間とともに変化し、シミュレーションが収束すると定常になります。一様な $p(\\mathbf{s})$ より Well-tempered "
"Target Distribution "
"の方が速く収束する場合があることが示されています（[こちら](http://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00076) "
"を参照）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:120
msgid "The System: Association/Dissociation of NaCl in Aqueous Solution"
msgstr "対象系：水溶液中の NaCl の会合・解離"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:122
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we will consider the association/dissociation of NaCl in "
"aqueous solution. The system consists of 1 Na atom, 1 Cl atom, and 107 water"
" molecules for a total of 323 atoms. In an effort to speed up the "
"simulations, we employ a rather small water box, and thus need to employ "
"smaller cutoffs than usually used. Therefore, this simulation setup should "
"not be used in production runs. Typically, the run should take around 15-20 "
"minutes to run on a laptop using two MPI processes. By running the "
"simulations on a cluster, you reduce the simulation time."
msgstr ""
"この Tutorial では、水溶液中の NaCl の会合・解離を扱います。系は Na 原子1個、Cl "
"原子1個、水107分子、計323原子です。高速化のため水の Box をかなり小さくし、通常より小さい Cutoff "
"を使います。この設定は本計算には使用しないでください。Laptop で2つの MPI Process "
"を使った場合、通常約15〜20分かかります。Cluster 上で実行すれば時間を短縮できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:124
msgid ""
"The most relevant CV for this system is the distance between the Na and Cl "
"atoms that is defined in PLUMED as"
msgstr "この系で最も重要な CV は Na と Cl の原子間距離で、PLUMED では次のように定義します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:131
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the NaCl association/dissociation is coupled to the collective "
"motion of the solvent. To measure that, we will use a CV that measures the "
"solvation of the Na atom. For this, we employ the coordination number of the"
" Na atom with respect to the oxygens of the water molecules that we define "
"in PLUMED as"
msgstr ""
"さらに、NaCl の会合・解離は溶媒の集団運動と結び付いています。その測定に Na 原子の Solvation を表す CV "
"を使います。水分子の酸素に対する Na 原子の Coordination Number を用い、PLUMED で次のように定義します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:148
msgid ""
"We will also limit CV space exploration by employing an upper wall on the "
"distance between Na and Cl atoms that is defined in PLUMED as"
msgstr "また、Na と Cl の原子間距離に Upper Wall を設け、CV 空間の探索を制限します。PLUMED では次のように定義します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:164
msgid "Exercise 1: Biasing with One Collective Variable"
msgstr "演習1：1つの Collective Variable に Bias を加える"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:166
msgid ""
"We will start by performing a simulation where we bias the Na-Cl distance."
msgstr "まず Na-Cl 距離に Bias を加えるシミュレーションを実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:168
msgid "Every VES simulation has three key ingredients:"
msgstr "VES シミュレーションには3つの重要な要素があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:170
msgid "Basis set"
msgstr "Basis Set"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:171
msgid "Target distribution"
msgstr "Target Distribution"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:172
msgid "Optimization algorithm"
msgstr "最適化アルゴリズム"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:174
msgid ""
"For the basis set, we will use the recently introduced [wavelet-based basis "
"set](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00197) that are localized basis "
"functions that have been shown to perform better than the previously used "
"Chebyshev or Legendre polynomials. We will employ the least asymmetric "
"variant of these wavelets or so-called symlets (as indicated by the "
"`TYPE=SYMLETS` keyword). We will use an order 10 of the symlets or Sym10 (as"
" indicated by the `ORDER=10` keyword). Furthermore information about the "
"wavelets can be found in the reference above."
msgstr ""
"Basis Set には、最近導入された [Wavelet に基づく Basis "
"Set](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00197) を使います。これらは局在した Basis "
"Functions で、従来の Chebyshev や Legendre 多項式より優れた性能が示されています。Wavelet "
"のうち非対称性が最も小さい Symlets を使います（`TYPE=SYMLETS` で指定）。次数は10、すなわち Sym10 "
"とします（`ORDER=10` で指定）。Wavelet の詳細は上記の文献を参照してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:176
msgid ""
"We need to select the range on which the bias potential is expanded. Here we"
" will use the range from 0.2 nm to 0.7 nm (as indicated by the `MINIMUM=0.2`"
" and `MAXIMUM=0.7` keywords). We also need to select the number of basis "
"functions, and here we will use 26 basis functions (as indicated by the "
"`NUM_BF=26` keyword). The PLUMED action corresponding to this setup is given"
" by"
msgstr ""
"BiasPotential を展開する範囲を選ぶ必要があります。ここでは0.2 nm から0.7 nm "
"とします（`MINIMUM=0.2`、`MAXIMUM=0.7` で指定）。Basis Functions "
"の数も選び、ここでは26個とします（`NUM_BF=26` で指定）。対応する PLUMED Action は次のとおりです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:206
msgid ""
"For the target distribution, we employ a well-tempered distribution with a "
"bias factor of 10."
msgstr ""
"Target Distribution には、Bias Factor 10の Well-tempered Distribution を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:240
msgid ""
"Then we define the VES bias potential using the `VES_LINEAR_EXPANSION` "
"action"
msgstr "次に `VES_LINEAR_EXPANSION` Action で VES の BiasPotential を定義します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:283
msgid ""
"Finally, we need to define the optimization algorithm. The standard is the "
"averaged stochastic gradient descent (`OPT_AVERAGED_SGD`). We need to define"
" two parameters: the stride and the step size. The stride (given by the "
"keyword `STRIDE`) is the number of MD steps in which samples are collected "
"to calculate the gradient and hessian of $\\Omega [V]$. The step size (given"
" by the keyword `STEPSIZE`) is the step by which the coefficients are "
"evolved at every optimization steps, given by $\\mu$ in the equation above. "
"It has become traditional to choose a stride of around 500-2000 MD steps. It"
" must be noted that we are not looking for an accurate estimation of the "
"gradient, since for this we would need to sample all the CV space. The step "
"size in the optimization has a strong connection with the height of typical "
"barriers in the system. The larger the barriers, the larger the step size "
"needed such that the bias can grow fast enough to overcome them. For this "
"example we have chosen a stride of 500 steps (i.e., 1 ps) and a step size of"
" 5.0 kJ/mol. We also need to choose how often we update the target "
"distribution (given by the keyword `TARGETDIST_STRIDE`) and we do this every"
" 100 bias potential updates (i.e., every 100 ps in the current case)."
msgstr ""
"最後に最適化アルゴリズムを定義します。標準は Averaged Stochastic Gradient Descent "
"(`OPT_AVERAGED_SGD`) です。Stride と Step Size の2つのパラメータが必要です。Stride（Keyword "
"`STRIDE`）は、$\\Omega [V]$ の勾配と Hessian を計算する Sample を集める MD Step 数です。Step "
"Size（Keyword `STEPSIZE`）は各最適化 Step で係数を更新する大きさで、上の式の $\\mu$ に対応します。Stride "
"は500〜2000 MD Step 程度がよく選ばれます。正確な勾配を推定しようとしているわけではありません。そのためには CV 空間全体の "
"Sampling が必要です。最適化の Step Size は、系の典型的な Barrier の高さと強く関係します。Barrier "
"が高いほど、それを越えるのに十分速く Bias を成長させるため、大きな Step Size が必要です。この例では Stride を500 "
"Step（1 ps）、Step Size を5.0 kJ/mol とします。Target Distribution の更新頻度（Keyword "
"`TARGETDIST_STRIDE`）も選び、BiasPotential の更新100回ごと（この場合100 ps ごと）とします。"

