msgstr ""
"`targetdistribution.<bias-name>.iter-<iteration-number>.data`：反復 <iteration-"
"number> の Target Distribution。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:438
msgid ""
"To assess the simulation and its convergence, you should first look at the "
"time evolution of the biased CV and check that it is diffusive in CV space. "
"Second, you should look at how the free energy surfaces behave as a function"
" of time by looking at the `fes.<bias-name>.iter-<iteration-number>.data` "
"files at different number of iterations (the minimum of the FES is always "
"aligned to zero to facilitate comparison). To do this, you need to use your "
"favorite way to plot datafiles (e.g., Matplotlib or Gnuplot). For instance, "
"you can use the `Analysis.ipynb` Jupyter notebook provided."
msgstr ""
"シミュレーションと収束を評価するには、まず Bias を加えた CV の時間発展を見て、CV 空間で拡散していることを確認します。次に、異なる反復数の "
"`fes.<bias-name>.iter-<iteration-number>.data` "
"を見て、自由エネルギー表面の時間変化を調べます（比較しやすいよう FES の最小値は常に0に揃えます）。Matplotlib、Gnuplot "
"など、好みの方法でデータファイルを描画してください。付属の `Analysis.ipynb` Jupyter Notebook も使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:443
msgid ""
"You can also visualize the trajectory by opening it with VMD by using the "
"command"
msgstr "次のコマンドで VMD を開き、Trajectory を可視化することもできます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:447
msgid ""
"The `NaCl_VES_NPT-300K.pbc-whole.xtc` is the trajectory file with the "
"periodic boundary conditions made whole. This is done within the `run.sh` "
"script."
msgstr ""
"`NaCl_VES_NPT-300K.pbc-whole.xtc` は、Periodic Boundary Conditions "
"で分断された分子をつなぎ直した Trajectory ファイルです。この処理は `run.sh` 内で行います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:449
msgid ""
"The `coeffs.data` file includes the values of coefficients "
"$\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ and $\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}$ at different "
"iterations. To extract the time evolution of a given coefficient, you can "
"use the `ExtractCoeff.sh` script, for example to extract coefficient 3:"
msgstr ""
"`coeffs.data` には、各反復での係数 $\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ と "
"$\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}$ が含まれます。特定の係数の時間発展は `ExtractCoeff.sh` "
"で抽出できます。例えば係数3を抽出するには、次のようにします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:455
msgid ""
"This will create a file with the first column the iteration number, the "
"second column the averaged coefficient $\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}$, and the"
" third column the instantaneous coefficients $\\boldsymbol\\alpha$. You "
"should create files for different coefficient and visualize both the second "
"and third columns to understand how the coefficients converge."
msgstr ""
"生成されるファイルの第1列は反復数、第2列は平均係数 $\\bar{\\boldsymbol\\alpha}$、第3列は瞬時係数 "
"$\\boldsymbol\\alpha$ です。複数の係数についてファイルを作り、第2列と第3列を可視化して収束の仕方を理解してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:461
msgid "Exercise 2: Reweighting a VES Simulation"
msgstr "演習2：VES シミュレーションの Reweighting"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:462
msgid ""
"Apart from estimating the FES directly from the bias potential, you can also"
" estimate the FES through reweighting by histogramming where each "
"configuration is weighted by the bias acting on it, $e^{\\beta "
"V(\\mathbf{s})}$. The VES bias acting at each time step is given by the "
"`ves.bias` variable in the `colvar.dat` file."
msgstr ""
"BiasPotential から直接 FES を推定するほか、各 Configuration に作用する Bias に応じて $e^{\\beta "
"V(\\mathbf{s})}$ で重み付けした Histogram を作り、Reweighting で FES を推定できます。各 Time Step"
" の VES Bias は `colvar.dat` の `ves.bias` 変数にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:467
msgid ""
"When doing performing reweighting, it is better to ignore the initial part "
"of the simulation where the bias potential is changing more rapidly. You can"
" use the `trim-colvar-file.py` python script in the Exercise-2 folder to do "
"this"
msgstr ""
"Reweighting では、BiasPotential が急速に変化する初期部分を除く方がよいでしょう。Exercise-2 の Python "
"スクリプト `trim-colvar-file.py` で処理できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:473
msgid ""
"where here we ignore the first 400 ps of the `colvar.data` file from the "
"Exercise 1 and create a new file called `colvar_reweight.data`."
msgstr "ここでは演習1の `colvar.data` の最初の400 ps を除き、`colvar_reweight.data` を作成します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:476
msgid ""
"We can then perform the reweighting for the distance using the following "
"PLUMED input (`plumed_reweight.dat` in the `Exercise-2` folder)"
msgstr ""
"次の PLUMED 入力（`Exercise-2` 内の `plumed_reweight.dat`）で距離について Reweighting できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:499
msgid "You can run this input by using the PLUMED driver"
msgstr "PLUMED driver でこの入力を実行できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:504
msgid ""
"You should compare the resulting FES (the `fes-reweight.dist.data` file) to "
"the results obtained directly from the bias potential in Exercise 1."
msgstr ""
"得られた FES（`fes-reweight.dist.data`）を、演習1で BiasPotential から直接得た結果と比較してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:507
msgid ""
"We can also obtain the FES for CVs that are not biased in the VES "
"simulation. For example, we can obtain the two-dimensional FES for the "
"distance and the solvation CV given by the coordination number CV. For this,"
" you will need to add the following to the plumed_reweight.dat file and "
"repeat the PLUMED driver run"
msgstr ""
"VES で Bias を加えていない CV の FES も得られます。例えば、距離と Coordination Number で表す Solvation"
" CV の2次元 FES を求められます。plumed_reweight.dat に次を追加して PLUMED driver を再実行してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:533
msgid ""
"Note that here we use kernel density estimation with Gaussian kernels to "
"obtain smoother results."
msgstr "ここでは滑らかな結果を得るため、Gaussian Kernel による Kernel Density Estimation を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:536
msgid ""
"You can also try to obtain the one-dimensional FES for the solvation CV by "
"adjusting the input above."
msgstr "上の入力を調整し、Solvation CV の1次元 FES を求めることも試してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:539
msgid "This will generate a two-dimensional FES that you can visualize."
msgstr "これにより、可視化できる2次元 FES が生成されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:541
msgid "Exercise 3: Running Another Independent Simulation"
msgstr "演習3：別の独立したシミュレーションの実行"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:543
msgid ""
"To check the results, it is a good practice to run another independent "
"simulation using different initial conditions. You can achieve this here by "
"changing the initial geometry in the `generate-tpr-file.sh` script"
msgstr ""
"結果の確認には、初期条件を変えて独立したシミュレーションを行うことが有効です。ここでは `generate-tpr-file.sh` "
"の初期構造を変更します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:549
msgid ""
"and regenerating the GROMACS tpr file. Do this and rerun the simulation, "
"check the convergence, and perform reweighting as before. Make sure that you"
" do this in a new clean folder that is separate from the run in Exercise 1."
msgstr ""
"その後、GROMACS tpr ファイルを再生成します。シミュレーションを再実行し、先ほどと同様に収束を確認して Reweighting "
"してください。演習1とは別の、新しい空のフォルダで実行してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:554
msgid "Exercise 4: Biasing with Two Collective Variables"
msgstr "演習4：2つの Collective Variables に Bias を加える"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:556
msgid ""
"We will now bias also the solvation CV. To achieve this, we need first to "
"setup a separate basis set for the solvation CV, where again we use the "
"symlets but with a different range from 2.0 to 8.0"
msgstr ""
"次に Solvation CV にも Bias を加えます。まず Solvation CV 用の別の Basis Set を設定します。ここでも "
"Symlets を使いますが、範囲は2.0〜8.0とします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:599
msgid ""
"We also need to change the relevant keywords in the `VES_LINEAR_EXPANSION` "
"action, namely the `ARG`, `BASIS_FUNCTIONS`, and `GRID_BINS` keywords"
msgstr ""
"また、`VES_LINEAR_EXPANSION` Action の `ARG`、`BASIS_FUNCTIONS`、`GRID_BINS` "
"を変更する必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:657
msgid ""
"Additionally, we have turned on the calculation of the one-dimensional "
"projection of the FES on the two CVs (we also need to set the keyword "
"`FES_PROJ_OUTPUT=100` in `OPT_AVERAGED_SGD`). This is useful to assess the "
"convergence as this is easier in one-dimension. We can also compare the "
"projection to the results from Exercise 1. These changes should be "
"sufficient to do the simulations using two CVs. You can see full input file "
"in the `Exercise-4` folder."
msgstr ""
"さらに、両 CV それぞれへの FES の1次元射影の計算を有効にしています（`OPT_AVERAGED_SGD` で "
"`FES_PROJ_OUTPUT=100` "
"も指定する必要があります）。1次元では収束を評価しやすいため便利です。射影を演習1の結果とも比較できます。これらの変更で2つの CV "
"を使うシミュレーションを実行できます。入力全体は `Exercise-4` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:665
msgid ""
"Once you have performed this simulation, you should also try to reweight "
"from this simulations. Furthermore, if you have time, you should also try to"
" perform another independent simulation."
msgstr ""
"実行後には、このシミュレーションからの Reweighting も試してください。時間があれば、別の独立したシミュレーションも実行してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:669
msgid "Optional Exercises"
msgstr "任意の演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:671
msgid ""
"The following three exercises are optional, but they will show you how "
"different parameters effect the results. You should base these exercises on "
"the files from the Exercise-1 folder and make the necessary changes. Make "
"sure that you run these simulations in separate folders and start from clean"
" files from the Exercise-1 folder."
msgstr ""
"以下の3つは任意ですが、パラメータが結果に与える影響を示します。Exercise-1 "
"のファイルを基に必要な変更を加えてください。それぞれ別フォルダで、Exercise-1 の未使用ファイルから開始してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:676
msgid "Optional Exercise 5: Play with the Optimization Parameters"
msgstr "任意演習5：最適化パラメータを変える"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:678
msgid ""
"The main parameter in the optimization algorithm is the step size and it is "
"not always easy to choose this parameter. Luckily, the algorithm is quite "
"robust and will work for different step sizes."
msgstr ""
"最適化アルゴリズムの主なパラメータは Step Size で、選択は必ずしも容易ではありません。ただしアルゴリズムは比較的頑健で、異なる Step "
"Size でも動作します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:682
msgid ""
"Run different simulations using step sizes 0.5 and 50.0 and try to "
"rationalize the behavior. Normally, when the step size is too large, the "
"system gets stuck in CV space and coefficients oscillate wildly. When the "
"step size is too small, the algorithm runs out of \"steam\" too fast and the"
" simulation converges slowly. These two extreme cases should be avoided."
msgstr ""
"Step Size を0.5と50.0にして別々のシミュレーションを実行し、挙動を説明してください。通常、大きすぎると系が CV "
"空間で動けなくなり、係数が激しく振動します。小さすぎるとアルゴリズムの推進力が早く失われ、収束が遅くなります。この両極端を避ける必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:688
msgid "Optional Exercise 6: Uniform Target Distribution"
msgstr "任意演習6：一様な Target Distribution"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:689
msgid ""
"Perform a simulation using an uniform target distribution and see how this "
"changes the results."
msgstr "一様な Target Distribution で実行し、結果の変化を調べてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:692
msgid "In this case, you need to change the target distribution to"
msgstr "この場合、Target Distribution を次のように変更します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:724
msgid ""
"and remove the `TARGETDIST_STRIDE` and `TARGETDIST_OUTPUT` keywords from the"
" \\ref OPT_AVERAGED_SGD action."
msgstr ""
"また、\\ref OPT_AVERAGED_SGD Action から `TARGETDIST_STRIDE` と "
"`TARGETDIST_OUTPUT` を削除します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:727
msgid "Legendre polynomials basis function"
msgstr "Legendre 多項式の Basis Functions"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:728
msgid ""
"Perform a simulation using Legendre polynomials (`BF_LEGENDRE`) basis "
"functions instead of the wavelets and see how this will affect the result. "
"As the Legendre polynomials are delocalized basis functions, this should "
"lead to more fluctuations in the bias potential as has been observed in the "
"[paper introducing the wavelets](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00197)."
msgstr ""
"Wavelet の代わりに Legendre 多項式 (`BF_LEGENDRE`) の Basis Functions "
"を使い、結果への影響を調べてください。Legendre 多項式は非局在の Basis Functions なので、[Wavelet "
"を導入した論文](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00197) で観測されたように、BiasPotential "
"の揺らぎが大きくなるはずです。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:733
msgid ""
"In this case, you need to change the basis set action in the PLUMED input to"
msgstr "この場合、PLUMED 入力の Basis Set Action を次のように変更します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:759
msgid "Additional comments"
msgstr "補足"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:761
msgid ""
"This should cover the basics of running VES simulations in PLUMED, but the "
"following comments might be of interest to some."
msgstr "ここまでで PLUMED による VES 実行の基礎を扱いました。以下の補足も参考になるでしょう。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:764
msgid "Restarting"
msgstr "再開"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:765
msgid ""
"VES simulations can be easily restarted. The code will automatically output "
"all the file needed at the end of the simulation. To restart, you just need "
"to reset the simulation with your MD code in the traditional way and add a "
"`RESET` keyword to the top of the PLUMED input (for some codes like GROMACS,"
" a restart is automatically detected by PLUMED and thus this keyword is not "
"needed)."
msgstr ""
"VES は容易に再開できます。必要な全ファイルはシミュレーション終了時に自動出力されます。通常の方法で MD コードの再開を設定し、PLUMED "
"入力の先頭に `RESET` を追加してください（GROMACS などでは PLUMED が再開を自動検出するため、この Keyword は不要です）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:771
msgid "Multiple Walkers"
msgstr "Multiple Walkers"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:773
msgid ""
"VES simulations supports the usage of multiple walkers where different "
"copies of the system share the same bias potential (i.e. coefficients) and "
"cooperatively sample the averages needed for the gradient and Hessian. This "
"can significantly help with convergence in difficult cases. It is of course "
"best to start the different copies from different positions in CV space. To "
"activate this option you just need to add the `MULTIPLE_WALKERS` keyword to "
"the `OPT_AVERAGED_SGD` action. Note that this is only supported if the MD "
"code support running multiple replicas connected via MPI (e.g., GROMACS or "
"LAMMPS)."
msgstr ""
"VES は、系の複数の Copy が同じ BiasPotential（係数）を共有し、勾配と Hessian に必要な平均を協力して Sampling "
"する Multiple Walkers に対応します。難しい系で収束を大きく改善できます。各 Copy は CV "
"空間の異なる位置から開始するのが望ましいでしょう。`OPT_AVERAGED_SGD` Action に `MULTIPLE_WALKERS` "
"を追加すれば有効になります。ただし、MPI で結ばれた複数の Replica の実行を MD コードがサポートする場合（GROMACS や LAMMPS"
" など）に限ります。"
